    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Projects</h2>
    <p>All tools are written in Rust, released under the Apache 2.0 license,
    and developed on <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift" target="_blank">Codeberg</a>.
    They form a pipeline: stng extracts strings, cleave performs deep static
    analysis, and litmus makes threat assessments using ML models trained on
    cleave output.</p>

    <ul class="proj-list">
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name"><a href="/cleave/">cleave</a></span>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">AST-aware software decomposition engine for supply-chain security. Detects capabilities and behaviors across 20+ languages and six binary formats in a single pass.</div>
        <div class="proj-links">
          <a href="/cleave/">Details</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/cleave" target="_blank">Source</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/cleave/issues" target="_blank">Issues</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name"><a href="/stng/">stng</a></span>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">Modern string extraction for binary analysis — all of the good stuff, none of the garbage. Useful for triage, C2 enumeration, credential extraction, and YARA signature development.</div>
        <div class="proj-links">
          <a href="/stng/">Details</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/stng" target="_blank">Source</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/stng/issues" target="_blank">Issues</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name"><a href="/litmus/">litmus</a></span>
        <span class="badge badge-beta">beta</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">ML-powered malware classifier for supply-chain security. Uses cleave static analysis to extract capabilities, then classifies threat level.</div>
        <div class="proj-links">
          <a href="/litmus/">Details</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus" target="_blank">Source</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus/issues" target="_blank">Issues</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name"><a href="/xgboost-native/">xgboost-native</a></span>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">Pure Rust XGBoost inference with exact TreeSHAP. No ONNX, no C++ runtime — runs anywhere Rust does.</div>
        <div class="proj-links">
          <a href="/xgboost-native/">Details</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift/xgboost-native" target="_blank">Source</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name">atomdrift</span>
        <span class="badge badge-planned">planned</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">Molecular drift detection. Tracks how code atoms shift across versions and dependencies.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>

